<title>TURKEY: Turkish Council of State cancels brokerage ruling.</title>
<headline>Turkish Council of State cancels brokerage ruling.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's Council of State cancelled a regulation introduced by the Capital Market Board (SPK) obliging banks in Turkey to set up or buy separate brokerage houses to handle their share transactions, an official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Turkey's bank union, two state and two private banks had applied to have the SPK regulation overturned after it was announced in October, the official said.</p>
<p>Most of the banks have already set up their own brokerage houses in line with the new regulation which was due to come into effect on January 2, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875</p>
